# Slice 334 (Codex review of 333, item 2): the receiver fn binds its arguments by the one binder of a call against its
# contracts -- ordinary signatures every traversal registers when it begins (fn: name, args, return, var, body; name,
# args, return, body; name, args, return; name, parts) --: by position and, for the parts of a receiver, by head.
# `fn: name: k1; args: ...` creates its function as the positional form does -- on entering the block, for its
# arguments are written -- with no callable named name here. A part given by head is its Frame whatever it holds (none,
# one field, a vertical block, a declaration, a statement). sub binds its own contracts by the same binder. Slice 335
# (Codex's answer to the 334 questions): a string literal gives a name by its value, its escapes decoded by the rules of
# C ("t\x33" names t3). M6 4a (slice 345; Codex CODEX-OPUS-345-4A-REPLY-20261110T041147Z-01 item 2): `part := (...)`
# gives no part any more (P0 refuses `:=` since 350) -- k1, k3, k4, s1, t1 and t3, written so before, are given by head with their values; this is
# the receiver's form of the implemented stage, not the declaration of edition 4 (`k1: fn: ...`, M6 3).
fn: name: k1; args: (int: a); return: int; body: (return: a + 1)
fn: name: k2; args: (int: a); return: int; body: (return: a * 3)
int: r1 k1(4)
int: r2 k2(4)
int: r3 k1(k2(1))
fn: name: k3; args: (int: a; int: b); return: int; var: (int: calls 0); body: (calls: calls + 1; return: a * 10 + b)
int: r4 k3(4; 2)
int: r5 k3(b: 1; a: 3)
int: c3 k3\var\calls
fn: name: k4; args: (); return: int; var: (int: n 7); body: (return: n)
fn: name: k5; args: (); return: int; var: (int: m 8); body: (return: m + 1)
int: r6 k4()
int: r7 k5()
fn:
    name: k6
    args:
        int: a
        int: b
    end: args
    return: int
    body:
        int: d a - b
        return: d * 2
    end: body
end: fn
int: r8 k6(9; 4)
sub: name: s1; args: (int: d 1); var: (int: total 0); body: (total: total + d)
s1(5)
s1()
int: total s1\var\total
fn: name: "t1"; args: (int: a); return: int; body: (return: a + 100)
fn: name: "t2"; args: (int: a); return: int; body: (return: a + 200)
fn: name: "t\x33"; args: (int: a); return: int; body: (return: a + 300)
int: r9 t1(1)
int: r10 t2(2)
int: r11 t3(3)
